{"slug":"viola-tricolor","plant":{"taxon":"Viola tricolor","family":"Violaceae","rank":"species","gbif_key":5331347,"wikidata":"Q190326","iucn":null,"gbif_occurrences":221539,"common_name":"Wild pansy","names":[{"source":"culpeper","name":"Heart’S-Ease","monograph_id":"cul:146-hearts-ease","confidence":"high","note":"Standard identification."}],"n_compounds":18,"top_compounds":[{"name":"β-carotene","qid":"Q306135"},{"name":"rutin","qid":"Q407857"},{"name":"lutein","qid":"Q422067"},{"name":"antheraxanthin","qid":"Q572404"},{"name":"violaxanthin","qid":"Q607883"},{"name":"violanthin","qid":"Q27108548"},{"name":"(15Z)-violaxanthin","qid":"Q27294499"},{"name":"Vicenin 2","qid":"Q104387517"}],"epmc_total":112,"trials":0,"claims":[{"concept_id":"syphilis","dsc":0,"cul":2,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.81,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"convulsions","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.83,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"epilepsy","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":1,"lift":1.37,"evidence_tier":"sparse"},{"concept_id":"itch_scabies","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":6,"lift":10.74,"evidence_tier":"studied"},{"concept_id":"pleurisy_pneumonia","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":1,"lift":1.28,"evidence_tier":"sparse"}],"lead_score":null},"texts":{"cul:146-hearts-ease":{"ref":"Culpeper, Complete Herbal: Heart’S-Ease","headword":"Heart’S-Ease","lang":"en","source":"culpeper","text":"The herb is really saturnine, something cold, viscous, and slimy. A strong decoction of the herbs and flowers (if you will, you may make it into syrup) is an excellent cure for the French pox, the herb being a gallant antivenereal: and that antivenereals are the best cure for that disease, far better and safer than to torment them with the flux, divers foreign physicians have confessed. The spirit of it is excellently good for the convulsions in children, as also for the falling sickness, and a gallant remedy for the inflammation of the lungs and breasts, pleurisy, scabs, itch, &c. It is under the celestial sign Cancer.","spans":[{"start":188,"end":191,"concept_id":"syphilis","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":218,"end":230,"concept_id":"syphilis","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":241,"end":254,"concept_id":"syphilis","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":435,"end":446,"concept_id":"convulsions","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":476,"end":492,"concept_id":"epilepsy","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":523,"end":548,"concept_id":"pleurisy_pneumonia","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":562,"end":570,"concept_id":"pleurisy_pneumonia","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":572,"end":577,"concept_id":"itch_scabies","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":579,"end":583,"concept_id":"itch_scabies","polarity":"therapeutic"}]}},"images":[]}